{
  "_doc": "Model tiers and initial traits for every agent. The three tiers are the single place to change models: `bin/stack agents tiers --apply` renders tier -> model id into each agent's frontmatter (env vars ADVANCED_MODEL / MEDIUM_MODEL / LOW_MODEL override the ids). effort and maxTurns here are INITIAL traits (maxTurns is a moderate allowance, ~2x a typical demanding run: enough headroom that demanding work is not cut short before the learner has evidence, without inviting runaway loops): they are written only when missing or with --reset-traits; afterwards the Bayesian learner (config/learning.json) owns them. 'alias' is what callers pass as the per-call `model` override of the Agent tool, which accepts only aliases.",
  "tiers": {
    "ADVANCED_MODEL": {
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "alias": "opus"
    },
    "MEDIUM_MODEL": {
      "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
      "alias": "sonnet"
    },
    "LOW_MODEL": {
      "model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
      "alias": "haiku"
    }
  },
